WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.749
Specialization divides work so people can develop
expertise.

2
00:00:03.949 --> 00:00:07.481
Horizontal specialization groups activities across
units.

3
00:00:07.681 --> 00:00:11.063
Vertical differentiation establishes levels of
authority.

4
00:00:11.263 --> 00:00:14.643
Horizontal does not automatically mean a flat hierarchy.

5
00:00:14.843 --> 00:00:16.894
Our workshop crosses several functions.

6
00:00:17.094 --> 00:00:23.556
Programs staff agree on the topic, public services
handles registration, and technical support checks
equipment.

7
00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:28.491
Each group can do its own task well while the overall
experience still fails at a handoff.

8
00:00:28.691 --> 00:00:30.717
A function describes a kind of work.

9
00:00:30.917 --> 00:00:35.595
A process follows related activities toward an outcome,
often across departments.

10
00:00:35.795 --> 00:00:40.098
Trace the workshop from request, through preparation, to
delivery and follow-up.

11
00:00:40.298 --> 00:00:42.129
Where does information need to move?

12
00:00:42.329 --> 00:00:43.916
Who notices when it does not?

13
00:00:44.116 --> 00:00:50.757
Libraries can group work by function, territory,
product, customer, process, subject, or form of
resources.

14
00:00:50.957 --> 00:00:53.417
Different groupings offer different advantages.

15
00:00:53.617 --> 00:00:59.428
A branch arrangement can bring service closer to users;
a subject department can build deep expertise.

16
00:00:59.628 --> 00:01:01.862
Both still need connections with other units.

17
00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:05.487
The design should serve the whole result, not just tidy
boxes.

